what's up everyone  Mike McCarty here with a GameSpot news  update developer Treyarch has shed a  little more light on why black ops 3 DS  campaign didn't make it into the last  gen versions of the game in a recent  interview creative director jason  blundell said the power of the last  generation machines was simply not  enough to deliver an uncompromised  version of what Trey art had in mind for  4 player co-op in the interview with  official Xbox Magazine blundell said  let's imagine I have my customized  weapons for you as a co-op player to see  what weapon I have you have to have  loaded in every single weapon  customization in the memory current gen  memory just can't do that you have to  have everything loaded otherwise you  just can't see what I'm carrying  blundell also said it would have been  possible to simplify things but this  could have had its own downsides as well  he went on to say I think Activision  made the right choice because I would  hate for people to get an experience  that wasn't true to the vision of it as  the director I'm incredibly passionate  about the experience being a pure one  the last gen versions of black ops 3 in  development at V Knox and mercenary  technology will run at 30fps compared to  60fps on new generation systems NTC  which are both being developed by  Treyarch black ops 3 for Xbox 360 and  ps3 launches November 6th alongside the  new gen and PC editions it comes with a  free copy of the original Call of Duty  Black Ops and sell for $50 instead of  the current gen $60 price tag well at  least the last gen version isn't  retailing at full price but if you are a  huge call duty fan it might be time to  make the jump to current gen for more  news and our review on black ops 3 stay  tuned to Gamescom  [Music]
 

